00:27:15,853 --> 00:27:22,853
あー 恋に落ちたまゆら 開花止まらないや 何度も捲って 心をかし
Ah, falling in love for a moment, flowering won't stop, turning pages again and again, charming the heart.

314
00:27:23,353 --> 00:27:29,853
泣いてばっかったの それがどうだ今や 腹よじるくらい笑う
I used to do nothing but cry, but look at me now, laughing till my stomach hurts.

315
00:27:30,353 --> 00:27:33,553
ずっと一緒に笑う
We'll laugh together forever.

316
00:27:33,853 --> 00:27:40,853
きみが持ってる 白い花に あたし見合わない かなしみになる
The white flower you hold doesn't suit me, bringing sadness.

317
00:27:41,353 --> 00:27:48,353
無垢な恋とか 正しさとか 誰も教えてくれなかった
Innocent love, righteousness... No one ever taught me about them.

318
00:27:48,853 --> 00:27:55,853
昨日会ったばっかで 今日もどこか会えたら なんて思う暮らし つつましくないよね
We just met yesterday, yet wishing to see you again today... What a modest life, isn't it?

319
00:27:56,353 --> 00:28:03,553
全部許されたの びっくりしちゃってさ 涙あふれていたよ
Everything was forgiven, taking me by surprise... My tears were overflowing.

320
00:28:04,353 --> 00:28:11,553
もう要になる花歌 透き通った空に 手を繋いでいった 夢のしるし
A humming melody becoming vital, in the clear sky, holding hands... A mark of a dream.

321
00:28:11,853 --> 00:28:18,853
どんな前世だってさ 忘れたっていいんだ きみと笑えるなら
Whatever past life it was, it's fine to forget it, as long as I can laugh with you.

322
00:28:19,353 --> 00:28:26,353
心が触れるたび 綺麗な音鳴る 目と目が合って くすぐったいね
Every time our hearts touch, a beautiful sound rings, our eyes meet and it feels ticklish.

323
00:28:26,553 --> 00:28:30,153
なんでもないこと 妙につぼるね
Smallest things oddly bring a smile to our faces.

324
00:28:30,353 --> 00:28:36,353
全部教えてくれて ありがとう
Thank you for teaching me everything.

325
00:28:49,353 --> 00:28:56,153
きみが持ってる 白い花を あたしの紅色と合わせたら
If I combine the white flower you hold with my crimson color...

326
00:28:56,353 --> 00:29:03,353
霜が溶けては 愛が行く もう寒くないよ
As the frost melts, love moves forward... It's not cold anymore.

327
00:29:08,853 --> 00:29:15,853
あー 恋に落ちたまゆら 開花止まらないや 何度も捲って 心をかし
Ah, falling in love for a moment, flowering won't stop, turning pages again and again, charming the heart.

328
00:29:16,353 --> 00:29:22,853
泣いてばっかったの それがどうだ今や 腹よじるくらい笑う
I used to do nothing but cry, but look at me now, laughing till my stomach hurts.

329
00:29:23,353 --> 00:29:30,353
ずっと一緒に笑って
Laughing together forever...

330
00:29:30,853 --> 00:29:36,353
心をかし
Charming the heart.

331
00:29:36,853 --> 00:29:40,353
ずっと一緒に笑う
Laughing together forever...

332
00:29:40,553 --> 00:29:45,353
最後の日を笑う
Laughing on our final day.

333
00:29:55,853 --> 00:30:00,353
これは、遠い遠い名も知らぬ世界で、
This is in a far, far away world with no name...

334
00:30:02,041 --> 00:30:05,841
死の呪いがかけられた少女のお話
A story of a girl who was cast with a curse of death.

335
00:30:26,241 --> 00:30:31,441
遠い遠い時の果て そこに住まう人は
Far, far away at the end of time, the people living there...

336
00:30:31,441 --> 00:30:37,441
皆永遠の命をもつ世界での話
This is a story of a world where everyone possesses eternal life.

337
00:30:37,441 --> 00:30:44,641
赤い実の成る木の下 La La Lu La 生まれながらに
Beneath the tree bearing red fruit, La La Lu La, from the moment she was born...

338
00:30:44,641 --> 00:30:51,441
死の呪いがかけられた少女のお話
This is the story of a girl cursed with death.

339
00:31:00,441 --> 00:31:09,141
色付いた街外れ 蒼く光る湖畔 赤い実のお菓子屋
On the colorful outskirts, by the blue-glowing lakeside, lies a red fruit sweet shop.

340
00:31:09,141 --> 00:31:17,141
ちょっぴり寒くなった今日は妙に誇らしげ 自新作を売りに行く
Feeling a bit chilly today, yet strangely proud, she sets off to sell her latest creation.

341
00:31:17,141 --> 00:31:25,141
待ってて 今度こそ美味しいんだから
"Just wait, because this time it's truly delicious!"

342
00:31:25,441 --> 00:31:32,441
時計塔の見える市 驚いた 珍しく賑やかね
At the market overlooking the clock tower, she's surprised—how unusually bustling it is!

343
00:31:32,441 --> 00:31:37,141
La La Lu La Lucky!! 物憂げな街の隅 ひとり
La La Lu La Lucky!! Alone in a melancholy corner of the town,

344
00:31:37,141 --> 00:31:42,441
赤い実のパイどうですか 自新作なの
"How about a red fruit pie? It's my pride and joy!"

345
00:31:42,441 --> 00:31:49,641
そんなのひとりも売れないさ 少女を見て蔑む人達
"Not a single one of those will sell," say the people looking down on the girl.

346
00:31:49,641 --> 00:31:57,141
みんなと何も変わらないのに 美味しくできたのに
"Even though I'm no different from anyone else, even though I made them so tasty..."

347
00:31:57,141 --> 00:32:01,641
今日も声は届かないのね
Today as well, my voice doesn't reach anyone, does it?

348
00:32:01,641 --> 00:32:05,641
まるで透明になったみたいだわ
It's as if I've become completely invisible.

349
00:32:05,641 --> 00:32:10,141
そうして誰もが知らぬふりをした
And so, everyone pretended not to notice.

350
00:32:10,141 --> 00:32:14,441
何故なら少女は呪われているから
Because the girl is cursed.

351
00:32:14,441 --> 00:32:22,141
死んだ世界で唯ひとり生きていた少女の話
The story of a girl who lived all alone in a dead world.

352
00:32:30,141 --> 00:32:38,141
夜なべでアレンジパイと にっこりスマイル引っ提げ 少女はまだ諦めない
Working through the night on new pie recipes, armed with a bright smile, the girl still won't give up.

353
00:32:38,141 --> 00:32:44,641
時計塔の針も空を指してお腹も鳴るそんな時
Just as the clock tower's hands point skyward and her stomach rumbles,

354
00:32:44,641 --> 00:32:52,841
ふと後ろから人が少女を押す 甘い籠は落ちる
Suddenly someone bumps into the girl from behind, spilling her sweet basket.

355
00:32:52,841 --> 00:32:59,141
お菓子を踏み行く人達 平気な顔してさ
People walk by, stepping over the sweets with nonchalant expressions.

356
00:32:59,141 --> 00:33:06,141
惨めに拾い集める ふともうひとりの手が
As she miserably gathers them up, suddenly another pair of hands joins in.

357
00:33:06,141 --> 00:33:14,141
とろとろのパイを徐に口に入れて「おいしいね」
Placing a messy pie into his mouth, he says, "It's delicious."

358
00:33:14,141 --> 00:33:18,441
その声で心は溢れた
With those words, her heart overflowed.

359
00:33:18,441 --> 00:33:22,641
まるで輪郭を描いたみたいだわ
It was as if her outline had finally been drawn.

360
00:33:22,641 --> 00:33:27,141
そうして彼は手を差し出した
And then, he reached his hand out to her.

361
00:33:27,141 --> 00:33:31,441
何故なら少女に呪われているから
Because he was enchanted by the girl.

362
00:33:31,441 --> 00:33:41,141
死んだ世界で唯ふたり生きていた遠い物語
A distant tale of two who lived together in a dead world.

363
00:33:51,441 --> 00:33:57,441
街の人達は哀れむ 赤い実を食べて呪われた者を
The townspeople pity those cursed from eating the red fruit.

364
00:33:57,441 --> 00:34:08,441
永遠に生きられずに死ぬのさ 嗚呼なんて可哀想な話
"They can't live forever, they will die! Ah, what a tragic story," they cry.

365
00:34:08,441 --> 00:34:15,141
ふたりは笑う それでも笑う
Yet the two laugh, smiling through it all.

366
00:34:15,141 --> 00:34:21,441
La La La とっても素敵な呪いね
La La La, what a wonderful curse it is.

367
00:34:21,441 --> 00:34:34,641
例え明日死んでも『今』が確かで大切になるから
Because even if we die tomorrow, "now" becomes real and precious.

368
00:34:36,141 --> 00:34:39,841
もう声は届かないのね
No voices can reach them anymore.

369
00:34:39,841 --> 00:34:44,141
まるで透明になったみたいだわ
It's as if they've become completely invisible.

370
00:34:44,141 --> 00:34:48,641
そうして誰もが知らぬふりをした
And so, everyone pretended not to notice.

371
00:34:48,641 --> 00:34:54,141
何故なら世界が呪われているから
Because the world itself is cursed.

372
00:34:54,141 --> 00:34:58,841
『永遠』の呪いは解かれていた
The curse of "eternity" was lifted.

373
00:34:58,841 --> 00:35:01,641
まるでふたりの方が狂ったみたいだろう
It must seem as though the two of them were the ones who went mad.

374
00:35:02,722 --> 00:35:06,922
そうしていつか笑うように眠る
And so, sleeping as if to smile someday,

375
00:35:06,922 --> 00:35:11,222
何故ならふたりは放たれているから
because the two of us have been set free.

376
00:35:11,222 --> 00:35:21,222
死んだ世界で唯ふたりだけが幸せだった
In a dead world, only the two of us were happy.

377
00:36:12,522 --> 00:36:17,522
さて、今日はこれくらいにしておきましょう、
Well then, let us wrap things up for today.

378
00:36:17,522 --> 00:36:20,522
…そろそろ時間になりましたし
...It's about that time, after all.

379
00:36:20,522 --> 00:36:24,522
…え？どこへ向かうのかって？
...Huh? Where am I heading, you ask?

380
00:36:24,522 --> 00:36:29,222
今日は何の日かご存知ないのですか？
Don't you know what day it is today?

381
00:36:29,222 --> 00:36:35,922
今日は、この王国の地下深くにある冥界でのハロウィンパーティーですよ！
Today is the Halloween party in the Underworld, deep beneath this kingdom!

382
00:36:35,922 --> 00:36:40,522
死者と生者が楽しむ年に一度のお祭りです、
It's a once-a-year festival enjoyed by both the dead and the living.

383
00:36:40,522 --> 00:36:44,522
さぁ、一緒に向かいましょう、
Now, let's head over together!

384
00:36:44,722 --> 00:36:46,522
でも、気を付けて、
But be careful.

385
00:36:46,522 --> 00:36:50,722
パーティーとはいえ、死者が住まう冥界です、
Party or not, it's the Underworld where the dead dwell.

386
00:36:50,722 --> 00:36:55,922
誰かの思念や死者たちによって奇妙な事が起こるかもしれませんが、
Strange things may happen due to someone's thoughts or the dead themselves,

387
00:36:55,922 --> 00:37:00,922
でも、決してそちらに耳を傾けすぎてはいけませんよ…
but you must never pay too much heed to them...

388
00:37:00,922 --> 00:37:04,722
それでは、参りましょう
Well then, let us go.

389
00:37:12,222 --> 00:37:16,222
蒼炎
[Blue Flame]

390
00:37:49,722 --> 00:37:53,522
誰かが言いました
Someone once said,

391
00:37:53,522 --> 00:37:57,522
激しく燃えるものほど
"The more intensely something burns,

392
00:37:57,522 --> 00:38:00,722
煌めく引き換えに
in exchange for its radiance,

393
00:38:00,722 --> 00:38:05,222
その身をすぐ焦がしきると
the sooner it burns itself out completely."

394
00:38:12,722 --> 00:38:16,722
数ある燭台に
Upon the numerous candlesticks,

395
00:38:16,722 --> 00:38:20,522
お好きな火を灯しましょう
let us light whichever flame you like.

396
00:38:20,522 --> 00:38:23,722
期待と裏腹に
Contrary to expectations,

397
00:38:23,722 --> 00:38:27,922
燻ればお生憎様
if it smolders, then what a pity.

398
00:38:27,922 --> 00:38:29,722
ランランランラン
La la la la,

399
00:38:29,722 --> 00:38:31,722
右手には錆びた時計
a rusty clock in the right hand.

400
00:38:31,722 --> 00:38:33,522
ランランランラン
La la la la,

401
00:38:33,522 --> 00:38:35,922
左には油の筒
a can of oil in the left.

402
00:38:35,922 --> 00:38:37,522
ランランランラン
La la la la,

403
00:38:37,522 --> 00:38:42,722
蠟のドレスを着飾って さあ
adorned in a dress of wax, come now.

404
00:38:42,722 --> 00:38:46,522
激しく 儚く
Intensely, fleetingly,

405
00:38:46,522 --> 00:38:50,722
蒼く燃ゆる花びら
blue burning petals.

406
00:38:50,722 --> 00:38:54,722
瞬き ゆらめく
Flickering and swaying,

407
00:38:54,722 --> 00:38:58,222
生を彩り照らせ
illuminate and color life,

408
00:38:58,222 --> 00:39:05,222
いずれ尽き果てる未来へと
toward a future that will eventually burn out.

409
00:39:09,522 --> 00:39:12,522
ゆりかごの目の前で
Right before the cradle,

410
00:39:12,522 --> 00:39:16,922
遙く飛び交う銃弾
bullets fly back and forth far away.

411
00:39:16,922 --> 00:39:24,522
指だけ動かせば容易くその火は潰える
With just a move of a finger, that flame easily dies out.

412
00:39:39,722 --> 00:39:46,922
仮初めの情熱で焼け爛れた舌では
With a tongue scorched by temporary passion,

413
00:39:46,922 --> 00:39:54,722
上手に喋ることができないようで
it seems unable to speak properly.

414
00:39:54,722 --> 00:40:01,522
喉元すぎても毒を孕ませて
Even after passing down the throat, harbored in poison,

415
00:40:01,722 --> 00:40:02,722
やがては 肺を腐らせる
eventually rotting the lungs.

416
00:40:03,477 --> 00:40:09,877
やがては肺を腐らせるでしょう
Eventually, it will rot your lungs.

417
00:40:10,677 --> 00:40:13,477
ランランランラン 揺らぐ死と生の狭間
Swaying between life and death,

418
00:40:13,677 --> 00:40:17,477
ランランランラン 焼ける心と歌う
I sing with a burning heart.

419
00:40:17,677 --> 00:40:24,677
ランランランラン 描いた最愛の終幕を
Praising the beloved finale I envisioned.

420
00:40:26,677 --> 00:40:33,177
激しく 儚く 蒼く燃ゆる花びら
Fiercely and fleetingly, blue burning petals...

421
00:40:33,477 --> 00:40:40,877
瞬き ゆらめく 生を彩り照らせ
Flickering and wavering, illuminate and color life.

422
00:40:41,177 --> 00:40:48,677
いずれ尽き果てるその先へ
Towards what lies beyond eventual exhaustion.

423
00:41:05,477 --> 00:41:11,177
あちらの世界に引きずり込まれないうちに早く会場へ向かわないといけませんね。
Before we get dragged into that world, we must hurry to the venue.

424
00:41:11,477 --> 00:41:13,677
気をつけてついてきてくださいね、
Please follow carefully,

425
00:41:13,777 --> 00:41:17,677
あまり深入りすると、おっと…
if you pry too deep, oops...

426
00:41:18,477 --> 00:41:22,177
そうそう、知らないほうがきっと懸命ですよ
That's right, it's probably wiser not to know.

427
00:41:22,877 --> 00:41:27,477
なんだかすっごく心地が良いよね
Somehow, it feels really comfortable, doesn't it?

428
00:41:44,677 --> 00:41:49,177
気づけば見知らぬ世界に立っていた
Before I knew it, I was standing in an unfamiliar world.

429
00:41:49,477 --> 00:41:54,677
何処かも分からず 毎日 毎日 毎日 泣いていた
Without knowing where I was, I cried day after day.

430
00:41:54,877 --> 00:41:55,977
なんて暇もなく
Without even time for that...

431
00:41:56,077 --> 00:41:58,477
Happy Time! おかしな面々が
Happy Time! Strange faces...

432
00:41:58,677 --> 00:42:01,177
Happy Time! おどけて転がるの
Happy Time! fooling around and tumbling.

433
00:42:01,277 --> 00:42:05,677
Happy Time! その馬鹿馬鹿しさに 希望も恐怖もなくなった
Happy Time! In that absurdity, both hope and fear vanished.

434
00:42:05,877 --> 00:42:13,677
確かそうアタシには 為すべき仕事 愛の棲家 パンプキン ヘッドギア
To be sure, I had work to do, a home of love, pumpkin headgear...

435
00:42:13,877 --> 00:42:21,477
だけどなんかどーでもいい
But somehow, none of it really matters.

436
00:42:22,677 --> 00:42:30,477
さぁ始まった 夢の夜だ 音楽が響いて 鳴り止まない 声を揃えて 叫べ今日は
Now it's begun, a night of dreams! Music echoes without stopping! Raise your voices and shout today!

437
00:42:30,577 --> 00:42:33,477
AMAZING HAPPY HALLOWEEN NIGHT

438
00:42:33,677 --> 00:42:40,477
ジャック いたずら 無礼講だ 真面目に生きても 割に合わない なんでもありさ 何故って今日は
Jack, tricks, anything goes! Living seriously isn't worth it, anything goes, because today is...

439
00:42:40,577 --> 00:42:43,477
AMAZING HAPPY HALLOWEEN NIGHT

440
00:42:43,677 --> 00:42:48,677
消えちゃった！ 消えちゃった！ 出口はないんだって そう 永遠に
Gone! Gone! They say there's no exit, yes, forever!

441
00:42:48,777 --> 00:42:53,477
消えちゃった！ 消えちゃった！ 思想 ルール 倫理 関係ない
Gone! Gone! Ideology, rules, ethics—none of it matters!

442
00:42:53,677 --> 00:42:56,477
AMAZING HAPPY HALLOWEEN NIGHT

443
00:42:57,477 --> 00:43:01,677
「私はロボットではありません」に
To 'I am not a robot',

444
00:43:01,877 --> 00:43:07,177
無心でチェックし解答するけれど 本当にそうかな
I mindlessly check and answer, but is that really true?

445
00:43:07,477 --> 00:43:10,177
Happy Life! とりま音に乗せて
Happy Life! For now, ride the sound,

446
00:43:10,277 --> 00:43:13,177
Happy Life! デタラメに踊るの
Happy Life! dance randomly.

447
00:43:13,277 --> 00:43:18,177
Happy Life! その繰り返しの中 懐疑心もしなった
Happy Life! In that repetition, even doubt withered away.

448
00:43:18,277 --> 00:43:25,177
意思のない様 まるで ロボトミーした電気羊
Devoid of intention, just like a lobotomized electric sheep.

449
00:43:25,477 --> 00:43:29,177
ナイトメア NPC
Nightmare NPC,

450
00:43:29,477 --> 00:43:33,477
だけどなんか心地が良い
but somehow, it feels good.

451
00:43:33,677 --> 00:43:34,877
What?

452
00:43:34,977 --> 00:43:37,477
おっと音声が乱れました
Oops, the audio got distorted.

453
00:43:37,577 --> 00:43:40,477
お気にになさらずに皆々様
Don't mind it, everyone.

454
00:43:40,577 --> 00:43:43,477
そんなお口は縫い合わせて
Sew those mouths shut,

455
00:43:43,577 --> 00:43:45,477
AMAZING HAPPY HALLOWEEN NIGHT

456
00:43:45,577 --> 00:43:48,177
良い子の口にはチョコとキャンディ
Chocolate and candy for good kids' mouths,

457
00:43:48,277 --> 00:43:50,877
歯に衣着せてっちゃ 噛み合わない
mincing words won't mesh well.

458
00:43:50,977 --> 00:43:53,477
気を取り直し みんなでどうぞ
Pull yourselves together, everyone, please,

459
00:43:53,577 --> 00:43:55,677
AMAZING HAPPY HALLOWEEN NIGHT

460
00:44:06,677 --> 00:44:17,177
知っちゃった！ 知っちゃった！ 知っちゃった！ 知っちゃった！ 知っちゃった！ 知っちゃった！
I found out! I found out! I found out! I found out! I found out! I found out!

461
00:44:17,477 --> 00:44:22,177
全部 全部 理解した
I understood everything, everything.

462
00:44:22,477 --> 00:44:25,177
だから何も見たくねぇわ
So I don't wanna see anything at all.

463
00:44:25,477 --> 00:44:33,177
さぁ始まった 夢の夜だ 音楽が響いて 鳴り止まない 声を揃えて 叫べ今日は
Now it's begun, a night of dreams! Music echoes without stopping! Raise your voices and shout today!

464
00:44:33,277 --> 00:44:35,877
AMAZING HAPPY HALLOWEEN NIGHT

465
00:44:35,977 --> 00:44:43,177
ジャック いたずら 無礼講だ 真面目に生きても 割に合わない なんでもありさ 何故って今日は
Jack, tricks, anything goes! Living seriously isn't worth it, anything goes, because today is...

466
00:44:43,277 --> 00:44:45,877
AMAZING HAPPY HALLOWEEN NIGHT

467
00:44:46,177 --> 00:44:51,477
泣いちゃった！ 泣いちゃった！ 知らない方がきっと懸命ね
Cried! Cried! It's surely wiser not to know!

468
00:44:51,577 --> 00:44:56,477
泣いちゃった！ 泣いちゃった！ このパーティーに終わりはない
Cried! Cried! There is no end to this party!

469
00:44:56,577 --> 00:44:59,677
AMAZING HAPPY HALLOWEEN NIGHT

470
00:45:15,318 --> 00:45:17,618
トリック・オア・トリート！
Trick or Treat!

471
00:45:17,618 --> 00:45:19,618
お菓子をくれても
Even if you give us treats...

472
00:45:19,618 --> 00:45:22,418
イタズラはしちゃうよ！
...we're still gonna play tricks on you!

473
00:45:50,418 --> 00:45:51,518
ようこそ everyone
Welcome everyone

474
00:45:51,518 --> 00:45:54,018
身の毛もよだつこの spooky night
To this hair-raising spooky night

475
00:45:54,018 --> 00:45:56,018
腹の底まで浸れ
Soak in deep to your core

476
00:45:56,018 --> 00:45:57,718
kick & bass & hats & trumpet

477
00:45:57,718 --> 00:45:59,318
ランタンと swingin' beat
Lanterns and a swingin' beat

478
00:45:59,318 --> 00:46:01,118
赤い靴で踊り狂えば
If you dance like mad in red shoes,

479
00:46:01,118 --> 00:46:04,418
浮世の憂いも忘れられるでしょ
you can forget the woes of this fleeting world, right?

480
00:46:04,918 --> 00:46:07,918
近頃巷じゃ オバケよりも怖い人たち
Lately around town, people are scarier than ghosts

481
00:46:07,918 --> 00:46:10,118
増えすぎっちゃってすぐに
They've increased so much, and right away...

482
00:46:10,118 --> 00:46:12,018
1 out, 2 out, 3 out, KO!!

483
00:46:12,018 --> 00:46:14,718
コンプライアンスも厳しい目の世の中ですが
Even in a world strict about compliance,

484
00:46:14,718 --> 00:46:18,718
恐怖のリライト請け負います
we'll undertake the rewriting of terror.

485
00:46:18,718 --> 00:46:21,518
GIVE ME A CHERRY PIE それとも may I choke you up?
GIVE ME A CHERRY PIE, or may I choke you up?

486
00:46:21,518 --> 00:46:25,118
GIVE ME A FLOWY DRESS それとも may I stab you to death?
GIVE ME A FLOWY DRESS, or may I stab you to death?

487
00:46:25,118 --> 00:46:28,818
poison, rope, pumpkin cake, knife, scissors, raspberry flake

488
00:46:28,818 --> 00:46:32,218
choose one...

489
00:46:34,518 --> 00:46:35,918
『さぁ選んで』
"Now, make your choice."

490
00:46:35,918 --> 00:46:37,918
なんちって ドッキリ大成功！
Just kidding, total prank success!

491
00:46:37,918 --> 00:46:40,318
響くパンパカパンファンファーレで
With resounding fanfares blasting,

492
00:46:40,318 --> 00:46:42,918
にっこり笑っちゃってはいピース
smile brightly and say cheese!

493
00:46:42,918 --> 00:46:45,218
あー怖かったななんて
Saying "Ah, that was scary,"

494
00:46:45,218 --> 00:46:47,818
座り込んで涙目で
slumping down with teary eyes...

495
00:46:47,818 --> 00:46:50,418
笑う顔見たいな
I wanna see your smiling face!

496
00:46:50,418 --> 00:46:54,018
ちっちゃな箱の中の モンスターに怯えるくらいなら
If you're scared of monsters inside a tiny box,

497
00:46:54,018 --> 00:46:56,718
いつだってここにおいで
come over here anytime.

498
00:46:56,718 --> 00:47:00,818
もっとずっと本能的で楽しくなれる
You can have way more instinctive fun.

499
00:47:00,818 --> 00:47:04,618
恐怖と踊っちゃおうぜ
Let's dance with terror!

500
00:47:04,618 --> 00:47:07,518
躁鬱相転移でキマってカタシス
Hitting that manic-depressive shift, pure catharsis!

501
00:47:07,518 --> 00:47:11,618
もういっちょ感情ジェットコースターでゴキゲンデトックス
One more time on the emotional rollercoaster, happy detox!

502
00:47:26,218 --> 00:47:29,518
満月が暴く醜悪な本性
The full moon reveals ugly true natures.

503
00:47:29,518 --> 00:47:32,418
デタラメに杖振り回し hocus pocus
Randomly waving a wand, hocus pocus!

504
00:47:32,418 --> 00:47:36,618
劣等感を苗床に育つ呪いを
The curse that grows with inferiority as its seed bed—

505
00:47:36,618 --> 00:47:40,018
摘み取る術を知ってるかい？
do you know how to pluck it away?

506
00:47:40,018 --> 00:47:42,918
『迷える哀れな子羊たちよ』
"O pitiless lost lambs,"

507
00:47:42,918 --> 00:47:45,918
『お菓子が欲しいかい？ それともヤラレタキが欲しいかい？』
"do you want sweets? Or do you want a beating?"

508
00:47:46,318 --> 00:47:47,918
『永遠に求め続けるの？』
"Will you keep seeking forever?"

509
00:47:47,918 --> 00:47:50,118
『それならば、ずっと苦しいままだ』
"If so, you will suffer forever."

510
00:47:50,118 --> 00:47:52,618
『恐怖からの解放によって』
"Through liberation from fear,"

511
00:47:52,618 --> 00:47:55,118
『成し得る救いがあるのならば』
"if there is salvation to be gained,"

512
00:47:55,118 --> 00:47:56,518
『この目隠しはそのままでに』
"keep this blindfold just as it is."

513
00:47:56,518 --> 00:47:58,618
『さぁ、イタズラ完了』
"Now, prank complete."

514
00:47:58,618 --> 00:48:01,618
永遠に断ち切れない
Bound by a curse's potion...

515
00:48:01,618 --> 00:48:03,918
呪いのクスイに囚われ
...that can never be severed for eternity,

516
00:48:03,918 --> 00:48:06,718
朽ち果ててしまう前に
before rotting away completely...

517
00:48:06,718 --> 00:48:10,618
脳みそちょっと弄るだけであら不思議！
Just messing with your brain a bit, and oh how wondrous!

518
00:48:10,618 --> 00:48:15,818
こんなに気持ち良くて気分爽快
It feels so good and refreshing!

519
00:48:18,918 --> 00:48:21,518
なんちって ドッキリ大成功！
Just kidding, total prank success!

520
00:48:21,518 --> 00:48:23,918
響くパンパカパンファンファーレで
With resounding fanfares blasting,

521
00:48:23,918 --> 00:48:26,418
にっこり笑っちゃってはいポーズ
smile brightly and strike a pose!

522
00:48:26,418 --> 00:48:28,618
あー辛かったななんて
Saying "Ah, that was tough,"

523
00:48:28,618 --> 00:48:31,118
へたり込んで涙目で
collapsing down with teary eyes...

524
00:48:31,118 --> 00:48:34,018
笑う顔っていいな
A smiling face is so nice!

525
00:48:34,018 --> 00:48:37,518
もう苦しまなくていいよ こんなに頑張ったんだから
You don't have to suffer anymore, after trying so hard.

526
00:48:37,518 --> 00:48:40,318
ためらわずこっちにおいで
Come over here without hesitation.

527
00:48:40,318 --> 00:48:44,418
もうずっと本能的に気持ちいいだけの
I'll show you the goal where it just feels...

528
00:48:44,418 --> 00:48:48,118
ゴールを見せてあげる
...instinctively good forever.

529
00:48:48,118 --> 00:48:51,118
困窮極まってこそ光るカタシス
Catharsis shines brightest when hardship reaches its peak!

530
00:48:51,118 --> 00:48:55,118
もういっちょ因果ぜリセットでタマシイデトックス
One more time, reset all karma for a soul detox!

531
00:49:02,718 --> 00:49:08,718
いつかの、あったかもしれない世界の出来事までも、
Even events of a world that might have existed someday...

532
00:49:08,718 --> 00:49:13,318
この冥界ではこうして思念として漂っているんだね。
...drift as thoughts like this here in the underworld.

533
00:49:13,318 --> 00:49:19,618
あまり深入りしてはいけないよ、こういうのが一番たちが悪い
You shouldn't dig too deep; these kinds are the worst of all.

534
00:49:19,618 --> 00:49:24,618
私はただ、あなたを愛していただけ
I was simply loving you...

535
00:49:32,118 --> 00:49:38,818
物言わぬ唇に生気を吹き込んで、
Infusing vitality into these silent lips,

536
00:49:38,818 --> 00:49:43,318
今宵「あなた」は甦る。
tonight, "you" are revived...

537
00:49:43,318 --> 00:49:48,618
あの頃の姿で。
...in your form from back then.

538
00:50:11,726 --> 00:50:14,126
白肌の娘が咳をした。
The fair-skinned girl coughed.

539
00:50:14,126 --> 00:50:16,426
「この身体貴方に捧げるわ」
"I offer this body to you."

540
00:50:16,426 --> 00:50:18,426
白服の医者が囁いた。
The doctor in white whispered,

541
00:50:18,426 --> 00:50:20,426
「迎えに行くよ」
"I will come for you."

542
00:50:20,726 --> 00:50:22,726
白肌の娘は朽ち果てた。
The fair-skinned girl decayed,

543
00:50:22,726 --> 00:50:24,726
世界の誰にも見捨てられ、
abandoned by everyone in the world.

544
00:50:24,726 --> 00:50:26,726
白服の医者は憐れんで、
Pitied by the doctor in white,

545
00:50:26,726 --> 00:50:29,226
誰も知らない居場所で眠らせた。
he laid her to rest where no one knew.

546
00:50:29,226 --> 00:50:31,926
朽ちてもまだ
Though decayed, still...

547
00:50:31,926 --> 00:50:34,926
美しい顔で、
...with a beautiful face,

548
00:50:34,926 --> 00:50:37,926
ふたりしかない霊廟で、
in a mausoleum built for only two,

549
00:50:37,926 --> 00:50:40,726
医者は恋をした。
the doctor fell in love.

550
00:50:40,726 --> 00:50:43,426
それは永遠の恋か。
Is it eternal love?

551
00:50:43,426 --> 00:50:46,426
禁断の行為か。
Or a forbidden act?

552
00:50:46,726 --> 00:50:49,426
また逢いたいと願うだけ。
Just wishing to see you again...

553
00:50:49,426 --> 00:50:52,426
それが罪なのでしょうか。
Is that really a sin?

554
00:50:52,726 --> 00:50:55,426
物謂わぬ唇に
Into her silent lips,

555
00:50:55,426 --> 00:50:58,426
生気を吹き込んで、
breathing life into them,

556
00:50:58,726 --> 00:51:01,426
今宵ふたりは結ばれる。
tonight, the two are united,

557
00:51:01,426 --> 00:51:04,126
祝福もされずに。
without a single blessing.

558
00:51:15,726 --> 00:51:18,926
『腐り落ちた眼孔に青い硝子を』
"Blue glass for the decayed eye sockets,"

559
00:51:18,926 --> 00:51:21,926
『破れかけた腕に絹の肌を』
"silk skin for the torn arms,"

560
00:51:21,926 --> 00:51:24,926
『侵された内臓に綿のガーゼを』
"cotton gauze for the diseased organs,"

561
00:51:24,926 --> 00:51:27,926
『宝石で飾った白いドレスを』
"and a pure white dress adorned with jewels."

562
00:51:27,926 --> 00:51:30,426
朽ちゆくたび
Every time she decayed,

563
00:51:30,426 --> 00:51:32,926
取り繕って、
he patched her up,

564
00:51:32,926 --> 00:51:36,126
恋を騙って、また医者は
falsely claiming it as love, the doctor

565
00:51:36,126 --> 00:51:39,426
手を染め続けた。
continued to stain his hands.

566
00:52:02,726 --> 00:52:05,726
やがて暴かれたのは
Eventually, what was exposed

567
00:52:05,726 --> 00:52:08,726
醜い怪物で、
was a hideous monster,

568
00:52:08,726 --> 00:52:12,126
「それ」を作り上げた医者は
and the doctor who created "it"

569
00:52:12,126 --> 00:52:15,726
弁駁を叫んだ。
shouted his defense:

570
00:52:15,926 --> 00:52:18,726
「これは永遠の恋だ。
"This is eternal love.

571
00:52:18,726 --> 00:52:21,726
彼女の願望だ。」
It was her wish."

572
00:52:21,726 --> 00:52:24,926
死に行くと決めたお前らが
"Wasn't she the woman you abandoned,

573
00:52:24,926 --> 00:52:27,926
見棄てた女じゃないか
deciding to leave her to die?"

574
00:52:27,926 --> 00:52:30,926
嗚呼……哀しき花嫁。
Ah, sorrowful bride...

575
00:52:30,926 --> 00:52:33,726
物謂えぬままで、
Remaining unable to speak,

576
00:52:33,926 --> 00:52:36,726
今宵ふたりは裁かれる。
tonight the two are judged

577
00:52:36,726 --> 00:52:42,426
彼女を見棄てた人達の正義で。
by the justice of those who abandoned her.

578
00:52:42,726 --> 00:52:47,726
正しいのはだあれ？
Who is truly in the right?

579
00:53:24,726 --> 00:53:28,126
さて、ハロウィンパーティーもついにフィナーレ。
Now, the Halloween party is finally coming to its finale.

580
00:53:28,126 --> 00:53:34,726
ここで、ご参加くださった国民の皆様へ冥界からの「お土産品」のご紹介です！
Here, for all the citizens who participated, we introduce souvenir items from the underworld!

581
00:53:34,726 --> 00:53:37,726
お土産品は、全4種類。
There are 4 types of souvenir items in total.

582
00:53:37,726 --> 00:53:42,426
フルセットでご購入いただいた皆様には、特典もございます。
Those who purchase the full set will also receive special bonus items.

583
00:53:42,426 --> 00:53:44,926
ご一緒に詳しく見ていきましょう！
Let's take a closer look together!

584
00:53:44,926 --> 00:53:50,926
まず1つ目、今回の「冥界ハロウィンナイト」をイメージした、ワイドラバーマットです。
First, here is the wide rubber mat inspired by this Underworld Halloween Night!

585
00:53:50,926 --> 00:53:59,426
国王様の横には、冥界の女王の姿が。名を「ナイラ」というそうです。
Beside the King is the figure of the Underworld Queen, whose name is said to be Naira.

586
00:53:59,426 --> 00:54:08,426
冥界のハロウィンを存分に楽しんでほしいという気持ちを込めた彼女のイメージソングも、この後お披露目予定なので、お楽しみに！
Her image song, filled with the wish for everyone to fully enjoy Underworld Halloween, will be revealed shortly, so please look forward to it!

587
00:54:08,426 --> 00:54:12,926
素敵なイラストは、Matcha様に描いていただきました。
This lovely illustration was drawn by Matcha-sama!

588
00:54:12,926 --> 00:54:17,426
2つ目は、パスポート風FBKINGDOMシール帳です。
Second, we have the passport-style FBKINGDOM sticker book!

589
00:54:17,426 --> 00:54:22,726
このシール帳には、これからたくさんの思い出を記していきたいですね。
We hope to record many wonderful memories in this sticker book going forward.

590
00:54:22,726 --> 00:54:28,926
王国の軌跡として、国民の皆様も今後集めてみてはいかがでしょうか？
Why not collect stickers as a trace of our Kingdom's journey from now on, everyone?

591
00:54:28,926 --> 00:54:34,726
その一歩として、今回のキービジュアルのステッカーを1枚封入しております。
As a first step, a sticker of this key visual is included inside!

592
00:54:34,726 --> 00:54:39,926
3つ目は、SUKONBU FACTORYより、キングフブちゃんぬいぐるみです。
Third, from SUKONBU FACTORY, we have the King Fubu-chan plushie!

593
00:54:39,926 --> 00:54:45,926
こちらは、国王自らデザインをしており、とても愛らしいぬいぐるみとなっております。
This was designed by the King herself, making it an extremely adorable plushie.

594
00:54:45,926 --> 00:54:51,726
前回のVol.1のぬいぐるみをお持ちの方は、ご一緒に飾ってあげてくださいね。
If you have the previous Vol. 1 plushie, please display them together!

595
00:54:51,726 --> 00:54:55,426
4つ目は、王国リボンチャームです。
Fourth is the Kingdom Ribbon Charm!

596
00:54:55,426 --> 00:55:00,926
こちらは、司書である私の胸元のリボンが再現されております。
This reproduces the ribbon worn at the chest by me, the librarian.

597
00:55:02,214 --> 00:55:05,114
ペンライトに付けるもよしと
You can attach it to a penlight,

598
00:55:05,314 --> 00:55:07,414
多機能なリボンチャームとなっておりますので
making it a multi-functional ribbon charm,

599
00:55:07,614 --> 00:55:11,614
皆様の「推し活」とやらに、ぜひご活用ください！
so please feel free to use it for your "oshi activities" or whatever you call it!

600
00:55:13,414 --> 00:55:15,214
最後は特典のお知らせです
Lastly, here's an announcement regarding bonuses!

601
00:55:15,214 --> 00:55:20,114
フルセットご購入の方全員に、チェキ風ブロマイドカードを1つお付けいたします
Everyone who purchases the full set will receive one Instax-style bromide card.

602
00:55:20,414 --> 00:55:25,114
複製サインと、国王からのメッセージもあるそうですよ
It also includes a printed autograph and a message from the King!

603
00:55:25,614 --> 00:55:31,114
数量限定バージョンは、直筆サイン入りですので、皆様お早めに！
The limited-quantity version has a real handwritten signature, so get yours quickly!

604
00:55:31,614 --> 00:55:34,814
以上、今回のお土産品紹介でした！
That concludes our souvenir showcase for today!

605
00:55:35,914 --> 00:55:36,814
さて
Now then,

606
00:55:36,914 --> 00:55:39,814
この後は冥界の女王様をイメージした楽曲
up next is a song inspired by the Queen of the Underworld,

607
00:55:39,814 --> 00:55:42,614
『冥界Halloween Night!』のお披露目です
the unveiling of "Underworld Halloween Night!"

608
00:55:42,814 --> 00:55:44,614
楽し創された後は
After you've enjoyed yourselves,

609
00:55:44,614 --> 00:55:48,114
無事 王国へお帰りくださいね
please return safely to the Kingdom, okay?

610
00:55:48,614 --> 00:55:50,114
それでは！
Here we go!

611
00:56:05,514 --> 00:56:06,714
Welcome!

612
00:56:06,714 --> 00:56:07,614
さあ、踊ろうよ
Come on, let's dance!

613
00:56:07,614 --> 00:56:09,114
This is Halloween Night!

614
00:56:22,614 --> 00:56:25,314
冥界を挙げての Party (Party)
A party hosted by the entire Underworld (Party)

615
00:56:25,414 --> 00:56:28,414
ルール違反はダメです Warning (Warning)
Breaking the rules is not allowed, Warning (Warning)

616
00:56:28,514 --> 00:56:31,414
説明は一度きり (きり)
The explanation will only be given once (once)

617
00:56:31,514 --> 00:56:33,814
聞き逃せばあの世行き！
Miss it and you're going to the afterlife!

618
00:56:33,814 --> 00:56:35,014
冗談です♡
Just kidding!♡

619
00:56:35,114 --> 00:56:36,614
(いち！) お菓子を持って
(One!) Grab some sweets!

620
00:56:36,714 --> 00:56:38,214
(に！) 仮装して盛って！
(Two!) Dress up and turn it up!

621
00:56:38,314 --> 00:56:41,014
(さん！) 生者か死者かは隠す事！
(Three!) Keep whether you're living or dead a secret!

622
00:56:41,114 --> 00:56:42,614
(よん！) いつだって笑顔で
(Four!) Always keep a smile!

623
00:56:42,714 --> 00:56:44,214
(ご！) 油断禁物で
(Five!) Never let your guard down!

624
00:56:44,314 --> 00:56:47,614
最後の最後はご無事で帰る事♡
And at the very end, return home safely!♡

625
00:56:48,614 --> 00:56:51,414
独りきりじゃ つまらないわ
Being all alone is so boring.

626
00:56:51,514 --> 00:56:54,514
この退屈な王城の玉座で
On the throne of this boring royal castle,

627
00:56:54,614 --> 00:56:58,814
